    {
      "id": "cc000000-0000-0000-0000-0000000000f1",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -700,
        -60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 660,
        "height": 690,
        "content": "## Triage inbound Gmail and draft replies for review\n\nEach new email is classified, summarised and answered with a draft. Nothing is sent\nautomatically: a person approves every reply.\n\n### How it works\n1. The Gmail trigger picks up each new message; a Code node normalises sender, subject and body.\n2. The model returns a structured verdict: category (sales, support, billing, spam, other),\n   priority, sentiment, detected language, a one-line summary, a draft reply, and a\n   needs-human-review flag.\n3. A validation node coerces the output to allowed values and flags anything malformed.\n4. Spam is logged and stopped. Everything else becomes a Gmail draft plus a row in Google Sheets.\n5. High-priority and sales mail also trigger a Slack message.\n\n### Setup\n1. Gmail OAuth2 credential on the Gmail Trigger and Create draft reply nodes.\n2. An Anthropic credential on the Chat model node, or any chat model n8n supports.\n3. Google Sheets credential on the two Log nodes, and a variable TRIAGE_SHEET_ID holding the\n   id of a spreadsheet with a tab named email_triage.\n4. Optional: Slack credential and target channel on the Slack alert node.\n\nAllowed categories, priorities and thresholds are constants at the top of the validation node."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
